XECUTES pi instead of erroring","residual":"the ELF reports --version 0.0.0 while the host npm install is 1.5.0; version parity with the host pi was not established"},"acceptance_criteria":"The solver install location must be durable and its absence must be loud. (a) The daemon resolves pi from a path that survives /tmp cleanup (a durable ELF under $HOME or an explicit PI_BIN in the unit), OR the startup path re-materialises /tmp/pi from a durable source; (b) a missing solver is a startup ERROR (nonzero exit / refused start) or a FAILING check, never a soft `note:` log line; (c) `make check-deploy` (or a new `make check-solver`) FAILS when the resolved pi is absent or unexecutable, and PASSES once it is present; (d) a scratch solve on a DB copy completes or is killed by its own timeout — never `pi binary not found`. Prove by running the new check against a tree where /tmp/pi is absent (expect FAIL naming the missing solver) and present (expect PASS), plus one real scratch solve that reaches pi-agent.","foreman_note":"Tick's biggest find; fixed live in-tick (host state, not repo code). Filed so the durability half lands as code: the soft note is the defect that hid a 12h outage.","worker_status":"complete","worker_summary":"Host-state repair + evidence; the durable/loud-fail half is the acceptance criteria above.","guard_result":"n/a (host state)"}
